WEBVTT

00:00:02.250 --> 00:00:03.970
Shugo, shugo!

00:00:03.970 --> 00:00:06.290
Start it off with a Doki! It's Shugo Chara time!

00:00:06.290 --> 00:00:09.580
Oh no! Yaya has picked up a stray kitten!

00:00:09.580 --> 00:00:13.250
But unlike that other cat, Yoru, it's super cute!  {this will be a problem throughout the episode, as the sex of the cat is unspecified... It'll be neccessary to use gender neutral pronouns etc... If it becomes too much of a hassle, I think it would also be okay to arbitrary decide its sex to be a girl, as I don't think it'll effect anything}

00:00:13.250 --> 00:00:16.490
However, it seems it's been separated from its owner.

00:00:16.490 --> 00:00:18.790
This sounds like a job for Amu-chan! {this is non-literal but entirely appropriate, I think}

00:00:18.790 --> 00:00:21.190
Let's find its owner, everybody!

00:00:21.190 --> 00:00:22.430
Yeah!

00:00:22.430 --> 00:00:23.690
Doki!

00:00:35.140 --> 00:00:42.180
If you were to walk so the wind fluttered the edge of your cape,

00:00:42.180 --> 00:00:48.570
people would look up at you in quiet admiration.

00:00:48.820 --> 00:00:55.870
You can say spicy things like "it's not my style," if you want,

00:00:55.870 --> 00:01:02.290
but I know who you really are because I'm your friend!

00:01:02.290 --> 00:01:04.160
Stand! Bow! {these are the two things said by the class rep when the teacher enters at the start of the school day}

00:01:04.160 --> 00:01:05.690
Nice and orderly now!

00:01:05.690 --> 00:01:09.530
And once that's done,

00:01:09.530 --> 00:01:14.800
it's time to start the school day.

00:01:15.130 --> 00:01:22.420
I like Mondays because I can see all my friends.

00:01:22.420 --> 00:01:28.820
There's nothing wrong with being abnormally happy.

00:01:28.820 --> 00:01:35.990
At lunch break, we have tea in the Royal Garden,

00:01:35.990 --> 00:01:43.330
where I tell you all my secrets!

00:01:53.960 --> 00:01:59.450
{book}The Heart's Egg

00:01:56.010 --> 00:02:00.810
Every child has an egg within their soul. {this should be identicle to the original engrish opening, unfortunately...}

00:02:00.810 --> 00:02:06.210
This heart's egg cannot be seen with one's eyes. But as the child grows up, it vanishes.

00:02:06.680 --> 00:02:11.650
Among the eggs, some exist which end up losing their way.

00:02:13.170 --> 00:02:15.740
Whose egg am I?

00:02:15.740 --> 00:02:17.750
Where did I come from?

00:02:17.750 --> 00:02:19.660
Where should I go?

00:02:21.450 --> 00:02:23.090
I don't know.

00:02:23.090 --> 00:02:25.200
I have my egg right here-wan.

00:02:26.710 --> 00:02:29.420
I don't know. It's not me.

00:02:29.720 --> 00:02:32.700
Where is my owner?

00:02:32.700 --> 00:02:34.600
I'm lonely.

00:02:34.600 --> 00:02:37.020
I want to go home.

00:02:37.020 --> 00:02:40.340
In order to find his owner,

00:02:40.340 --> 00:02:43.790
the lost little egg went on a journey.

00:02:43.790 --> 00:02:45.830
What will they be like?

00:02:45.830 --> 00:02:48.190
I hope I meet them soon.

00:02:54.950 --> 00:02:58.490
What could our little black cat be doing?

00:03:01.800 --> 00:03:04.470
Perhaps he is still just as lost.

00:03:10.830 --> 00:03:15.790
Episode 94
Onward! The Calico Cat Search Party!?

00:03:17.340 --> 00:03:19.840
Yaya, what's that?

00:03:27.520 --> 00:03:29.310
A kitten!

00:03:29.310 --> 00:03:30.790
What's going on?

00:03:30.790 --> 00:03:34.150
I found it wandering around lost yesterday.

00:03:34.150 --> 00:03:36.730
Amu-chan, it's wearing a collar!

00:03:37.030 --> 00:03:39.190
You're right. So it's someone's pet?

00:03:39.530 --> 00:03:44.510
Must be, so I thought I should try to find its owner.

00:03:44.510 --> 00:03:47.380
But Yaya-tan's mom is allergic to cats.

00:03:47.380 --> 00:03:48.960
So that's why you brought it to school?

00:03:48.960 --> 00:03:53.570
I know it's not a good idea to bring a cat here, but...

00:03:54.160 --> 00:03:58.240
Hey, why don't we search for the kitten's owner together?

00:03:58.240 --> 00:04:00.160
Really? You'll help me?

00:04:00.160 --> 00:04:01.080
Of course.

00:04:01.080 --> 00:04:02.650
If not us, then who?

00:04:02.650 --> 00:04:05.030
Okay! We'll start the search after school.

00:04:05.030 --> 00:04:05.990
Great.

00:04:05.990 --> 00:04:08.560
Thanks, everyone!

00:04:08.860 --> 00:04:12.210
Kiseki, please take care of the kitten in the interim.

00:04:12.210 --> 00:04:14.560
If I must. Leave this to me.

00:04:14.860 --> 00:04:19.740
Don't take your eyes off it for a second, though. The teachers mustn't discover it.

00:04:19.740 --> 00:04:20.610
Okay!

00:04:20.910 --> 00:04:25.030
It sure would be helpful if Yoru was here right now.  {Can't you talk to animals, too?  Hey!}

00:04:25.030 --> 00:04:28.590
Do you think he's still on the hunt for Ikuto?

00:04:29.470 --> 00:04:33.080
Ikuto, where are you-nya?

00:04:34.570 --> 00:04:37.460
Where the heck are you-nya?

00:04:49.250 --> 00:04:50.180
Amu...

00:04:50.930 --> 00:04:52.350
Ikuto...

00:04:54.930 --> 00:04:55.850
Hey...

00:04:58.770 --> 00:05:02.150
What have you done to me?

00:05:03.960 --> 00:05:06.300
I'm not allowed to talk to you!

00:05:15.830 --> 00:05:17.730
You failed again?

00:05:17.730 --> 00:05:19.530
C-Correct!

00:05:19.530 --> 00:05:27.630
Just like the Mk. V, VI, VII, IIX, IX, X, the Come Here Embryo Mk. IV...

00:05:30.540 --> 00:05:33.100
...was a failure.

00:05:35.520 --> 00:05:41.380
I must gather a large number of X Eggs to test the validity of my theory.

00:05:41.380 --> 00:05:44.480
I suppose I have no choice but to use Ikuto.

00:05:46.820 --> 00:05:49.950
It sure has messed up the place.

00:05:50.930 --> 00:05:52.040
Did you find it?

00:05:52.040 --> 00:05:53.410
Nope-dechu!

00:05:53.720 --> 00:05:55.620
Here little kitty!

00:05:55.620 --> 00:05:57.300
Where are you?

00:05:57.300 --> 00:06:00.110
Show yourself! That's an order from the King!

00:06:04.690 --> 00:06:06.580
W-What are you doing?

00:06:07.700 --> 00:06:09.210
After it-dechu!

00:06:09.210 --> 00:06:10.090
Right!

00:06:16.110 --> 00:06:17.920
What's the matter, Yaya-chan?

00:06:17.920 --> 00:06:19.950
Are you not feeling well?

00:06:19.950 --> 00:06:22.110
Oh, I'm fine.

00:06:22.720 --> 00:06:25.990
I wonder how Kitty is doing?  {Yaya decides to call the cat "Neko-chan", which I will be translating as the name "Kitty"... this makes sense for a later convo.}

00:06:27.750 --> 00:06:28.820
What's this?

00:06:30.590 --> 00:06:31.910
Kitty!

00:06:31.910 --> 00:06:33.330
How cute!

00:06:35.930 --> 00:06:37.580
Quiet down, everyone!

00:06:38.940 --> 00:06:40.080
There it is!

00:06:40.350 --> 00:06:43.980
Pepe-chan, didn't we tell you to take good care of it?

00:06:43.980 --> 00:06:45.400
Yaya-chan?

00:06:45.400 --> 00:06:46.880
Who are you talking to?

00:06:47.590 --> 00:06:50.430
Um, well...

00:06:52.400 --> 00:06:54.560
I'm declaring a state of emergency!

00:06:57.000 --> 00:06:58.850
Guardian here, reporting for duty! {Ah yaya, always abusing your power...}

00:07:01.680 --> 00:07:03.900
And she's gone...

00:07:03.900 --> 00:07:06.440
Wait!

00:07:06.740 --> 00:07:08.010
That voice...

00:07:08.010 --> 00:07:08.650
Yaya?

00:07:11.970 --> 00:07:14.200
Hurry, Yaya-tan!

00:07:22.040 --> 00:07:23.960
Wait up already!

00:07:24.730 --> 00:07:27.690
Hinamori-san, we're in the middle of class here!

00:07:27.690 --> 00:07:30.550
Um, I've gotta... go to the bathroom...

00:07:30.550 --> 00:07:32.580
Be right back!

00:07:34.260 --> 00:07:36.300
Where could it have gone?

00:07:36.300 --> 00:07:37.430
Yaya!

00:07:37.870 --> 00:07:39.240
Amu-chan.

00:07:39.240 --> 00:07:40.380
Oh hey, guys.

00:07:40.380 --> 00:07:41.350
What are you doing?

00:07:41.650 --> 00:07:43.860
But Kitty...

00:07:43.860 --> 00:07:45.010
Yeah!

00:07:45.770 --> 00:07:47.690
Chairman's Office

00:07:48.150 --> 00:07:50.290
It sounded like it came from in here, right?

00:07:50.290 --> 00:07:51.430
Yeah.

00:07:53.870 --> 00:07:55.120
Pardon us...

00:07:57.090 --> 00:07:58.950
Aw, you like this?

00:07:59.550 --> 00:08:01.000
Um...

00:08:02.190 --> 00:08:04.100
Oh, this?

00:08:04.100 --> 00:08:07.500
You never know when you'll run into a little kitty cat, you know?

00:08:07.800 --> 00:08:11.010
Um, that's not what I meant...

00:08:11.010 --> 00:08:12.530
Hinamori-san.

00:08:14.930 --> 00:08:17.430
Care to explain?

00:08:21.230 --> 00:08:25.440
We want to look after it until we find its owner.

00:08:25.740 --> 00:08:27.940
Well, that sounds good and all, but...

00:08:27.940 --> 00:08:33.470
Nikaidou-sensei, I may have come up with a good idea.

00:08:34.820 --> 00:08:40.000
So you see, we Guardians decided to look for its owner.

00:08:40.000 --> 00:08:44.810
However, if possible, we'd like the representatives from each class to help out.

00:08:44.810 --> 00:08:45.960
We're in!

00:08:52.880 --> 00:08:55.570
Tsukushi-chan, Mao-chan, you came, too?

00:08:55.570 --> 00:08:56.430
Of course!

00:08:56.430 --> 00:08:58.910
We have to return it to its home quickly, don't we?

00:08:58.910 --> 00:09:01.670
What should we do first?

00:09:01.670 --> 00:09:05.800
How about we distribute "does anyone recognize this kitten" fliers?

00:09:05.800 --> 00:09:08.090
We should get it something to eat, too.

00:09:08.090 --> 00:09:09.990
Isn't this nice, Kitty?

00:09:09.990 --> 00:09:12.190
Everyone wants to help you.

00:09:12.190 --> 00:09:16.680
"Kitty?" Surely there's a better name for it.

00:09:16.680 --> 00:09:19.130
Yeah, I guess we should give it one.

00:09:19.130 --> 00:09:20.990
Just call it Kitty.

00:09:20.990 --> 00:09:22.120
But...

00:09:22.400 --> 00:09:25.450
It's someone's pet, right?

00:09:25.450 --> 00:09:28.010
It probably already has a name.

00:09:28.010 --> 00:09:30.840
I'd feel bad calling it something else.

00:09:31.430 --> 00:09:33.090
You have a point...

00:09:33.090 --> 00:09:37.290
So until we find its home, we'll just call it Kitty!

00:09:37.290 --> 00:09:39.210
Right, Kitty?

00:09:40.140 --> 00:09:42.030
I think it understands!

00:09:42.030 --> 00:09:43.100
For real!

00:09:46.330 --> 00:09:48.670
Yeah, wow.

00:09:48.670 --> 00:09:50.090
This should be perfect.

00:09:50.090 --> 00:09:51.410
Really?

00:09:51.410 --> 00:09:53.040
How about this design?

00:09:53.040 --> 00:09:54.780
It's so cute!

00:09:54.780 --> 00:09:58.410
Okay, so after the fliers are ready, we'll go hand them out.

00:09:58.410 --> 00:10:00.070
Just leave things here to us!

00:10:01.390 --> 00:10:03.440
I'm totally beat-nya...

00:10:03.440 --> 00:10:04.520
Oh, Yoru!

00:10:04.520 --> 00:10:07.060
Still looking for Ikuto, huh?

00:10:07.060 --> 00:10:11.110
Yeah, but I can't find him anywhere-nya!

00:10:11.110 --> 00:10:16.580
Ah, I guess it's not easy to find someone being held by Easter.

00:10:16.580 --> 00:10:23.920
Utau told me Easter's Director is her and Ikuto's stepfather,

00:10:23.920 --> 00:10:29.310
and that Ikuto's being forced to work for them to atone for their real father's sins.

00:10:31.400 --> 00:10:32.650
Ikuto...

00:10:33.150 --> 00:10:34.290
Amu-chan!

00:10:35.160 --> 00:10:37.740
Shall we get down to business?

00:10:37.740 --> 00:10:40.960
Let's do it! Yeah!

00:10:42.510 --> 00:10:44.280
Oh yeah?

00:10:44.280 --> 00:10:48.280
You got separated from your owner, too-nya?

00:10:48.280 --> 00:10:50.410
Okay! Understood-nya!

00:10:50.410 --> 00:10:53.070
I'll help, too-ny-

00:10:53.070 --> 00:10:56.310
Stop it-nya! Don't bite my tail-nya!

00:11:12.600 --> 00:11:16.780
Now then, ready to get to work, Ikuto?

00:11:18.570 --> 00:11:22.660
You know what will happen if you disobey me.

00:11:30.720 --> 00:11:33.420
Wow. You're really good at this.

00:11:33.420 --> 00:11:36.090
I want to be a carpenter when I grow up.

00:11:36.390 --> 00:11:37.500
Finished!

00:11:38.770 --> 00:11:40.370
I can't see the resemblance.

00:11:40.370 --> 00:11:43.560
Even its owner wouldn't be able to tell from this.

00:11:45.030 --> 00:11:46.670
You're really good!

00:11:45.740 --> 00:11:47.010
Wow!

00:11:47.010 --> 00:11:50.310
Found!
Seiyo Academy Elementary School

00:11:47.450 --> 00:11:49.680
She really captured its distinguishing features!

00:11:50.310 --> 00:11:52.420
Wow, it's the spitting image!

00:11:52.420 --> 00:11:53.640
It really is.

00:11:53.640 --> 00:11:56.130
Tsukushi wants to be a manga artist when she grows up.

00:11:56.130 --> 00:11:57.600
I can see why!

00:11:57.600 --> 00:11:59.650
No wonder you're so good.

00:12:00.540 --> 00:12:02.360
I bought milk!

00:12:02.360 --> 00:12:03.570
Sensei!

00:12:03.570 --> 00:12:06.390
Did you make sure it's appropriate for kittens?

00:12:06.390 --> 00:12:07.790
Something like that exists?

00:12:08.090 --> 00:12:10.140
You sure know a lot, Mao-chan!

00:12:10.140 --> 00:12:15.080
Of course! I'm aiming to be a veterinarian, so I study these things.

00:12:15.370 --> 00:12:18.960
It's really impressive that everyone has their own dreams.

00:12:30.090 --> 00:12:31.350
I can feel it...

00:12:31.350 --> 00:12:33.270
Yeah, their eggs.

00:12:33.270 --> 00:12:36.490
Everyone's hearts' eggs are...

00:12:36.490 --> 00:12:38.900
...sparkling nice and brightly-nya!

00:12:39.200 --> 00:12:40.570
Everyone's...

00:12:40.570 --> 00:12:42.640
...hearts' eggs?

00:12:43.880 --> 00:12:46.210
It must be because of Kitty!

00:12:46.210 --> 00:12:50.120
Thanks to Kitty's influence, their dreams are flourishing-dechu! {or widening, growing larger...}

00:12:54.060 --> 00:12:55.600
Pardon us.

00:12:58.680 --> 00:13:01.260
The Chairman isn't here...

00:13:06.190 --> 00:13:10.940
Every child has an egg within their soul...

00:13:13.490 --> 00:13:15.580
A lost egg?

00:13:17.770 --> 00:13:19.150
It's torn.

00:13:20.010 --> 00:13:22.030
A lost egg...

00:13:28.660 --> 00:13:30.160
Well, hello.

00:13:30.690 --> 00:13:32.240
Nice to see you.

00:13:33.870 --> 00:13:38.190
Now that I think about it, I've been running around so much I haven't properly introduced myself.

00:13:38.190 --> 00:13:40.760
Nice to meet you, Rhythm-kun.

00:13:40.760 --> 00:13:42.450
My name is Amakawa Tsukasa.

00:13:42.450 --> 00:13:43.920
Pleasure's mine!

00:13:44.210 --> 00:13:46.010
Where did you go?

00:13:46.010 --> 00:13:48.590
To buy some kitten supplies.

00:13:49.650 --> 00:13:52.120
Do you think it'll like these?

00:13:54.890 --> 00:13:57.350
So, can I help you with something?

00:13:57.350 --> 00:14:00.360
We were thinking of heading out to distribute the finished fliers.

00:14:00.360 --> 00:14:02.970
Great idea. Stay safe, okay?

00:14:04.740 --> 00:14:06.650
What's the matter?

00:14:06.650 --> 00:14:10.040
You wrote this story, correct?

00:14:10.040 --> 00:14:12.130
Why won't you repair it?

00:14:12.790 --> 00:14:15.460
How exactly does the story conclude?

00:14:17.540 --> 00:14:20.420
If it were you, how would you end it?

00:14:20.730 --> 00:14:26.420
Isn't imagining all the possible endings the best part of reading a story?

00:14:29.420 --> 00:14:30.890
I'm trying to find it...

00:14:30.890 --> 00:14:34.940
The conclusion to my own story.

00:14:37.310 --> 00:14:39.180
Please!

00:14:39.180 --> 00:14:41.800
Do you recognize this kitten?

00:14:41.800 --> 00:14:43.310
Please!

00:14:43.310 --> 00:14:44.550
Amu-chan!

00:14:44.550 --> 00:14:47.240
Think we should try asking her?

00:14:48.910 --> 00:14:54.830
"Gifted fortune-teller Saeki Nobuko's Miracle Luck-Changing Series! On sale now to rave reviews!"

00:14:54.830 --> 00:14:55.700
That's what it says.

00:14:56.000 --> 00:14:57.910
Oh, it's just a poster.

00:14:57.910 --> 00:15:01.550
You know, we haven't seen her for a while. I guess she was writing that book.

00:15:01.550 --> 00:15:04.210
Stop slacking off, guys-nya!

00:15:04.500 --> 00:15:07.990
I can understand feeling desperate, you know...

00:15:07.990 --> 00:15:12.890
That feeling of wanting to be with your owner as soon as you can...

00:15:13.190 --> 00:15:14.300
Yoru...

00:15:15.260 --> 00:15:18.320
I'm sure the owner wants to find it, too.

00:15:18.320 --> 00:15:21.210
They must be so worried.

00:15:21.210 --> 00:15:23.980
And I'm sure Ikuto is thinking of you, too, Yoru.

00:15:24.270 --> 00:15:26.790
Okay! Let's do this!

00:15:26.790 --> 00:15:28.590
Yay!

00:15:29.100 --> 00:15:30.600
I'll let you know if I find them.

00:15:30.600 --> 00:15:31.490
Thank you!

00:15:31.810 --> 00:15:33.610
Please!

00:15:33.610 --> 00:15:35.850
We're looking for its owner.

00:15:35.850 --> 00:15:37.270
Please help us!

00:15:37.270 --> 00:15:38.000
Sure.

00:15:38.300 --> 00:15:40.350
Please help us!

00:15:41.520 --> 00:15:43.250
How cute!

00:15:43.250 --> 00:15:44.980
It's like a stuffed animal!

00:15:44.980 --> 00:15:48.210
Shh... Be quiet...

00:15:54.520 --> 00:15:57.210
Amu-chan, it's getting late.

00:15:57.210 --> 00:15:58.880
I think we should call it a day.

00:15:58.880 --> 00:16:02.170
No, I'm going to keep trying a bit longer.

00:16:02.170 --> 00:16:04.540
Do you recognize this kitten-nya?

00:16:12.270 --> 00:16:15.440
Please...

00:16:20.020 --> 00:16:22.000
Everyone's hearts' eggs!

00:16:22.300 --> 00:16:23.490
It's Ikuto-nya!

00:16:23.490 --> 00:16:26.810
That sound means Ikuto's here-nya!

00:16:37.420 --> 00:16:40.010
Mao-chan, Tsukushi-chan!  {I presume we've never seen these two people before... They're in Yaya's class, and we don't know many people in that class.}

00:16:41.540 --> 00:16:43.110
Ikuto-kun...

00:16:50.290 --> 00:16:51.590
Ikuto!

00:17:03.160 --> 00:17:04.920
Amu-chan, Character Transform!

00:17:05.220 --> 00:17:06.490
But...

00:17:08.910 --> 00:17:09.960
Right.

00:17:12.340 --> 00:17:14.210
My heart:

00:17:14.210 --> 00:17:15.830
My heart:

00:17:15.830 --> 00:17:17.220
My heart:

00:17:17.520 --> 00:17:19.180
Unlock!

00:17:35.680 --> 00:17:38.320
Character Transformation: Platinum Royal!

00:17:39.620 --> 00:17:42.620
Character Transformation: Beat Jumper!

00:17:44.410 --> 00:17:47.210
Character Transformation: Amulet Heart!

00:17:57.410 --> 00:17:59.090
Ikuto, stop this!

00:17:59.910 --> 00:18:01.100
Ikuto!

00:18:01.400 --> 00:18:03.160
Can't you hear me?

00:18:04.350 --> 00:18:06.410
What are you doing, Ikuto?

00:18:06.410 --> 00:18:07.290
Ikuto!

00:18:07.290 --> 00:18:10.400
Yeah, stop it!

00:18:10.980 --> 00:18:12.070
Yaya?

00:18:13.200 --> 00:18:14.650
Everyone's...

00:18:15.180 --> 00:18:17.660
Everyone's hearts' eggs...

00:18:19.490 --> 00:18:21.740
They were sparkling so brightly, but now...

00:18:23.080 --> 00:18:25.490
Why would you do this?

00:18:25.490 --> 00:18:30.790
How could you hurt Mao-chan and Tsukushi-chan, and all of these kids with their eggs so full of dreams?

00:18:30.790 --> 00:18:32.520
It's cruel...

00:18:32.520 --> 00:18:33.710
Cruel!

00:18:34.010 --> 00:18:35.330
No-nya!

00:18:35.330 --> 00:18:38.030
Ikuto isn't cruel-nya!

00:18:38.030 --> 00:18:45.020
Yeah, we've done a lot of bad things-nya, but I know-nya...

00:18:45.020 --> 00:18:47.940
That Ikuto's really...

00:18:52.120 --> 00:18:53.440
Amu-chan!

00:18:54.170 --> 00:18:57.610
Blaze Shoot!

00:18:57.610 --> 00:18:58.750
Yoru!

00:19:01.570 --> 00:19:03.740
The X Egg energy is increasing!

00:19:04.040 --> 00:19:09.170
Incredible. This has far surpassed the number of X Eggs from the recording!

00:19:09.170 --> 00:19:12.670
If this continues, the Embryo will be here soon!

00:19:18.080 --> 00:19:19.300
Director...

00:19:20.530 --> 00:19:22.050
I...

00:19:23.660 --> 00:19:24.600
Ikuto?

00:19:24.830 --> 00:19:27.320
Amu-chi, the eggs!

00:19:36.450 --> 00:19:38.390
Platinum Heart!

00:19:57.590 --> 00:19:59.070
The Embryo!

00:19:59.070 --> 00:20:00.800
I knew it.

00:20:16.910 --> 00:20:18.740
Ikuto...

00:20:21.150 --> 00:20:24.120
What just happened?

00:20:24.120 --> 00:20:29.250
The Embryo does not appear merely by gathering a large number of X Eggs.

00:20:29.250 --> 00:20:32.110
It's when those X Eggs are purified that it shows itself.

00:20:36.390 --> 00:20:38.380
I see!

00:20:38.730 --> 00:20:41.560
And now, my theory has been proven.

00:20:45.580 --> 00:20:48.250
Huh? What happened?

00:20:55.800 --> 00:20:57.680
Please look at this!

00:20:58.650 --> 00:21:00.820
Do you recognize this kitten?

00:21:04.570 --> 00:21:06.440
Let's go, you guys!

00:21:09.900 --> 00:21:12.040
Um, have you seen this kitten before?

00:21:15.610 --> 00:21:18.170
Thank you so much, everyone!

00:21:18.510 --> 00:21:20.870
Don't get lost again, okay?

00:21:20.870 --> 00:21:22.670
Take care, Kitty!

00:21:23.750 --> 00:21:27.330
By the way, what's its name?

00:21:27.330 --> 00:21:30.220
It was just born, so it doesn't have one yet.

00:21:30.220 --> 00:21:33.390
I know! Why don't you choose a name for it?

00:21:34.460 --> 00:21:35.560
Are you sure?

00:21:35.820 --> 00:21:38.040
What do you think we should call it?

00:21:38.040 --> 00:21:39.290
Good question.

00:21:39.290 --> 00:21:40.640
Oh! Oh! I know!

00:21:40.640 --> 00:21:41.730
Tama-chan!

00:21:42.150 --> 00:21:43.560
Tama-chan?

00:21:43.560 --> 00:21:44.860
Isn't that just a bit too cliché?

00:21:45.160 --> 00:21:46.840
It's kind of...

00:21:46.840 --> 00:21:48.410
Just because it's a cat doesn't mean...

00:21:48.710 --> 00:21:53.150
No! It made all those hearts' eggs sparkle, right?

00:21:53.150 --> 00:21:55.420
So let's call it Tama-chan, from "tamago."

00:21:53.150 --> 00:21:57.620
Note: "Tamago" means egg.  {The reverse could be said that if they haven't figured that out by now, they are retards. - Asa I don't see why we can't put this note in.  It's so fundamental to the show anyway. Anyone who watches 90+ episodes deserves to know this word in Japanese by now :)}

00:22:00.230 --> 00:22:01.890
See ya later, Tama-chan!

00:22:01.890 --> 00:22:05.120
Have a nice life with your owner-nya!

00:22:27.870 --> 00:22:33.220
You sure do seem determined.

00:22:34.630 --> 00:22:39.270
So even if you screw up, it'll somehow turn out all right.

00:22:39.970 --> 00:22:46.640
How about you just trust in yourself?

00:22:46.920 --> 00:22:53.100
Take that first step and everything will work out fine.

00:22:53.710 --> 00:23:00.030
Even if people see through your cool exterior, keep marching on.

00:23:00.450 --> 00:23:09.110
Look up at the blue sky and everything will reset!

00:23:09.690 --> 00:23:12.750
Take it easy! Take it easy! {the first is in English, the second is in Japanese (but that is the exact same meaning)}

00:23:13.030 --> 00:23:23.290
Try to relax those shoulders and clear your mind.

00:23:23.290 --> 00:23:30.000
The more you do it, the easier it'll get, so keep taking it easy.

00:23:30.000 --> 00:23:35.200
Ride the flow of time and you'll be...

00:23:36.260 --> 00:23:39.000
Shining! Shining! Shining!

00:23:49.860 --> 00:23:54.450
Nanja Kunjyawa Charakan Bun Ken Hoi!

00:23:54.450 --> 00:23:56.260
Um, what's that supposed to mean?

00:23:56.260 --> 00:23:59.500
It's a spell that helps you find something you've lost.

00:23:59.500 --> 00:24:00.670
A spell?

00:24:00.670 --> 00:24:02.500
Can something like that actually help?

00:24:02.500 --> 00:24:05.130
No way. Ran just made it up.

00:24:05.130 --> 00:24:07.170
Bun Ken Hoi!

00:24:07.170 --> 00:24:07.900
Huh?

00:24:07.900 --> 00:24:10.160
Speaking of which, what are you looking for?

00:24:10.160 --> 00:24:12.460
Next time on Shugo Chara!! Doki:

00:24:12.460 --> 00:24:14.530
Rima, Yaya, and the Pearls that Bind Them. {note, a more literal translation would be "Rima And Yaya, The Pearls of Bondage" but I really would hesitate to title a SC episode with the word "bondage"...}

00:24:14.530 --> 00:24:17.240
I hope they have no trouble finding it.

00:24:17.240 --> 00:24:19.240
Find <i>what</i>?!
